               "caution":  "A single 8.03% rebound does not reverse a steep downtrend. ETN remains deeply below its $378.06 50-day and $389.40 200-day EMAs on lukewarm volume, meaning rallies toward $355 or $378 could meet fresh selling. Fundamentally, long-term debt doubled to $17.8 billion this year; if interest rates stay elevated or hyperscalers pause AI data center spending, both earnings multiples and deleveraging progress could face renewed pressure.",
