               "fundamental":  "Eaton\u0027s November 3 Q3 2026 report reinforced its core role in AI power infrastructure, supplying switchgear, UPS, busways, and now Boyd Thermal liquid cooling from grid to chip. Record revenue of $8.95 billion (+28% YoY; +19% organic), adjusted EPS of $3.68, and Electrical Americas margins reaching 29.8% (+230 bps sequentially as new capacity ramped) prove strong execution. Combined electrical backlogs topped $20.4 billion (+46% YoY), lifting full-year guidance to 13%–15% organic growth and $13.70–$13.80 adjusted EPS (implying $4.05–$4.15 in Q4). The trade-off is leverage: acquisition funding pushed long-term debt to $17.8 billion as of September 30, though $1.03 billion in Q3 free cash flow and roughly $1.1 billion in expected cash from the early-2027 Dana Mobility spin-off should help deleveraging. The electrical installed-base moat remains firmly intact.",
