                            "On November 18, 2026, Erste Group downgraded ETN from Buy to Hold after Q3 filings showed long-term debt doubled to $17.8 billion due to acquisitions. Earlier on November 11, Jefferies and JPMorgan initiated coverage at Neutral with $395 targets, while Bernstein raised its target to $534.",
                            "SEC Form 4 filings disclosed on November 23 showed open-market share purchases during the selloff by CEO Paulo Ruiz (300 shares at $322.63 on November 20) and CFO David Foster (200 shares at $346.24 on November 16 and 150 shares at $323.60 on November 20).",
                            "After sliding near its $308.22 52-week low on November 20 amid broader AI-industrial valuation compression, ETN rallied 8.03% on November 23 to $336.34 as dip buyers stepped in.",
