               "opportunity":  "For long-term AI-infrastructure holders, the roughly 30% drop from the $478.00 high reflects valuation compression and balance-sheet digestion rather than weakening demand. With over $20 billion in electrical backlog, triple-digit rolling data center order growth, and expanding capacity pushing Electrical Americas margins to 29.8%, operational momentum is accelerating. Pairing Boyd Thermal\u0027s liquid cooling with electrical switchgear—and shedding lower-margin Mobility assets via Dana in early 2027—positions Eaton as a focused grid-to-chip leader once technicals stabilize.",
               "opportunityCheck":  "The page\u0027s AI-opportunity sub-scores are broadly sensible, but AI revenue exposure now looks understated and warrants an upward adjustment. Q3 2026 data center revenue jumped 65% with rolling orders up over 100%, the March Boyd Thermal deal added direct liquid cooling for AI racks, and spinning off Mobility into Dana in early 2027 will structurally raise Eaton\u0027s electrical mix. Bottleneck and pricing power also lean slightly conservative given Electrical Americas\u0027 29.8% margin and $20 billion-plus backlog, while market growth, position, and optionality look appropriately calibrated.",
