               "technical":  "ETN\u0027s chart remains technically bearish despite an 8.03% rebound to $336.34 on November 23. Price sits well below its key Exponential Moving Averages (EMAs — trend lines weighting recent prices): 11.0% under the 50-day EMA ($378.06), 13.6% under the 200-day EMA ($389.40), and 14.0% under the 100-day EMA ($391.07). With the 50-day EMA below the 200-day EMA, the medium-term trend points downward. Momentum indicators confirm caution: MACD (a trend-momentum gauge comparing two EMAs) sits at -17.65 below its -16.52 signal line with a negative -1.13 histogram, while RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) recovered only to 41.93, still below the 50 midpoint. Within Bollinger Bands (a volatility channel around the 20-day average), ETN bounced off the $309.48 lower band but remains below the $354.85 middle band and in the bottom fifth of its $308.22–$478.00 52-week range. Volume of 3.50 million shares barely topped the 3.41 million 20-day average (+2.7%), and the intraday fade from $342.50 shows supply near resistance ($355, then $378–$391) above $308–$310 support."
